# Fixture: simple-cubic single-atom lattice (a = 3.0 Ang), 3D bulk, no vacuum
# axis. Simple-cubic connectivity is BIPARTITE (2-colorable: a checkerboard
# makes every nearest-neighbor pair unlike), so the AB-ordered representative
# reaches the ideal -1.0 pair correlation exactly (README section 1.4) -- the
# clean contrast to the frustrated FCC (GaAs) and triangular (MoS2) cases.
# --sublattice Na --species-b K substitutes it into a Na(1-x)K(x) toy alloy.
# (A fixture for stb-gqca's Stage 1 only; no real DFT is run on it.)

NumberOfSpecies    1
NumberofAtoms      1

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   11   Na
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 3.0000000000   0.0000000000   0.0000000000
 0.0000000000   3.0000000000   0.0000000000
 0.0000000000   0.0000000000   3.0000000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
 0.000000000   0.000000000   0.000000000   1
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
